            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Crossing balloons:&quot; a new technique for complex angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>980-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new technique is described for complex percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty of a lesion at the bifurcation of the obtuse marginal branch of the left coronary artery, just distal to a venous bypass graft insertion. Two separate angioplasty guide wire and catheter systems were used and the coronary artery side branch was protected in a &quot;crossing&quot; manner.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
